Z||000031||Oreif||11-15-2000||02:34 PM||||First you need to read the 3.75 box was 30 X 12 X 18 and I corrected it in the second post to 26 X 12 X 16. Next I went to the Rockford site and looked it up. 12" HX2 VAS is 4.238 which is calculates to 1.0595 minimum volume size required for the speaker to function properly. RF recommends 1.25 for perfect operation. The Infinity VAS is 4.932 which requires 1.233 cu ft of volume. (Infinity's site.) If my "designs" are so wrong how come the boxes work so well?  <BR>Why don't you give me the exact speaker you are going to use and the box dimensions (inside dimensions) and we'll see how your math works. You keep changing speakers every post. (Eclipse, Infinity, Rockford)<P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-15-2000).]||||reg||1
