Z||000036||Oreif||11-15-2000||06:22 PM||||I did admit that 30 X 12 X 18 was too big. That is why I changed it to 26 X 12 X 16.<BR>Do you actually read posts or just scan them?<BR>Someone please remind me NOT to take engineering courses at his school. (or go to the stereo shop he worked at) The Infinity Kappa Perfect 12 Requires 1.2 cu ft per speaker. If your building a box that is .65 cu ft (per speaker) that is too small. Eclipse may be different since I don't know which model you want. For a set of 12" subs with high power I wouldn't use fiberglass.  A Fiberglass box will resonate just like a plywood box. (by resonate I mean the box itself will produce unwanted sound) MSD wood is better for the larger woofers with lots of power.  It's always those who think they are higher looking down that in reality haven't a clue which way is up.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
