Z||000055||Seanh||11-15-2000||10:52 PM||||Wow, I should have checked this thread sooner, look at all the fun I have been missing. Jonny, I currently work at a fairly well known high-end stereo shop, here in Nebraska. I'm an installer, not all that good at subbox designes, so I asked my fellow workers to take a look at your "concepts". First of all, Oreif is correct, althought wrong with the size of your design in his first post, he is correct about the box sizes. They also dont think your design will be hitting 150db, or even close with your idea. My baby hits at about 147bd, thats running 2 Polk Momo 12's behind the seats, 1 Polk Momo 10" up front, and one Polk Db 8 under dash. I would really like to see you out do me in a stereo comp. with your idea.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>88/2.8, I really like Pioneer headunits. Mine is a Premier, but pretty much the same. DEH-P900R. I love it. Pioneer is a really great company to deal with. Although, you couldnt pay me to use a Pioneer Amp in a good system. The only ones I use are the Premier PRS series because of their power supplies. Did you get it hooked up okay? Can be kinda a pain with the stock Performance sound system option. I really need to post some information about it on my website.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
