Z||000058||Oreif||11-16-2000||10:18 AM||||You can put your speakers in a smaller than designed box, BUT Placing speakers in a box smaller than they were designed for will cause you to lose sound. SPL (sound pressure level) and tonal quality of a speaker is based on the ability of the cone to move in an efficent manner. A smaller box will increase pressure behind the speaker. This will limit cone movement. Since the frequency of the cone moving is what produces the sound and the distance the cone moves is what produces the SPL, Dampening this will cause your SPL to drop and lower frequencies will not be produced. By compensating with "killer power" you would be forcing the speaker to operate at pressures greater than the design of the speaker. This excessive pressure will now distort the cone and stress the weakest part of it. (usually the outside suspension foam)<BR>Eventually the foam ring will tear to release the pressure and then the cone will not have the support and distort even more. If you put two 12" subs in a box roughly 1.5 cu ft, I'll bet that one 8" sub in a properly designed box would sound better. Sound quality and SPL go hand in hand. Without one the other suffers. So I will put an 8" sub in my car and you put the two 12's (in a 1.5 cu ft box) in yours. Then we'll pick a place in between our homes that has an IASCA competition. We can than have both vehicles tested for SPL and sound quality using a real time analyzer.<BR>I've got $1000.00 dollars says I'll score higher than yours in both areas.<P>Electrical engineering won't help. Take some courses in physics and mechanical design.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||13
Z||000059||stimpy||11-16-2000||11:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jonny_blaze:<BR><B>people should just stay out of my conversations.  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, if you want to act the fool and not have anyone comment, then confine your threats to <B>private e-mail</B>,the forum is no place for it. I personally don't care what size box you use, hell, it's your car, do whatever you want. My <B>suggetion</B> is that you put your d!ck away and keep things more friendly then this. You may need someone someday.  ||||reg||1
